One of the nice things about getting a spellbook as a gift is
that it is blessed.  Otherwise, yes.  As a Valk, reading
spellbooks is something for the later parts of the game, when
the risk is not that great.  But then, a Valk won't have the
power to cast spells much until the late game anyway, and many
of the most important things you'd want the spells for (cure
sickness when meeting Pestilance, magic missles for watery
levels, etc.) are also late game considerations.

And of course, if you've price-id'ed the book, you can generally
read the less expensive ones.  Two of the most useful (for any
character), cure sickness and remove curse are 300 base cost,
light is only a 100 (very useful if you have jumping boots---if
not jumping is also 100).

